      "description": "Write a function that takes a byte, swaps its halves (like the example) and\nreturns the result.\n\nYour function must be declared as follows:\n\nunsigned char    swap_bits(unsigned char octet);\n\nExample:\n\n1 byte\n_____________\n0100 | 0001\n\\ /\n/ \\\n0001 | 0100"
    },
    "referenceCode": "/* ************************************************************************** */\n/*                                                                            */\n/*                                                        :::      ::::::::   */\n/*   swap_bits.c                                        :+:      :+:    :+:   */\n/*                                                    +:+ +:+         +:+     */\n/*   By: jcluzet <jo@cluzet.fr>                     +#+  +:+       +#+        */\n/*                                                +#+#+#+#+#+   +#+           */\n/*   Created: 2017/07/20 21:01:37 by fwuensch          #+#    #+#             */\n/*   Updated: 2021/07/02 16:27:22 by jcluzet          ###   ########.fr       */\n/*                                                                            */\n/* ************************************************************************** */\n\n#include <unistd.h>\n\nunsigned char\tswap_bits(unsigned char octet)\n{\n\treturn ((octet >> 4) | (octet << 4));\n}\n",
    "mainCode": "#include <unistd.h>\n\nunsigned char\tswap_bits(unsigned char octet);\n\nint\tmain(int argc, char **argv)\n{\n\tunsigned char c;\n\n\tc = argv[1][0];\n\twrite(1, &c, 1);\n\twrite(1, \"\\n\", 1);\n\tc = swap_bits(c);\n\twrite(1, &c, 1);\n\twrite(1, \"\\n\", 1);\n\treturn (0);\n}\n",
